          "heading": "Subjects",
          "heading_path": [
            "Subjects"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "ev_passage_736affac48f80799",
        "source_type": "passage",
        "provider": "direct_http",
        "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-024-08449-y",
        "document_id": null,
        "title": "Quantum error correction below the surface code threshold | Nature",
        "snippet": "Quantum computing promises computational speed-ups in quantum chemistry[5](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR5 \"Aspuru-Guzik, A., Dutoi, A. D., Love, P. J. & Head-Gordon, M. Simulated quantum computation of molecular energies. Science 309, 1704–1707 (2005).\"), quantum simulation[6](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR6 \"Lloyd, S. Universal quantum simulators. Science 273, 1073–1078 (1996).\"), cryptography[7](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR7 \"Shor, P. W. Polynomial-time algorithms for prime factorization and discrete logarithms on a quantum computer. SIAM Rev. 41, 303–332 (1999).\") and optimization[8](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR8 \"Farhi, E. et al. A quantum adiabatic evolution algorithm applied to random instances of an NP-complete problem. Science 292, 472–475 (2001).\"). Howeve",
        "content_ref": "f2ebbac237a8314a6ed7b1200d535d5bfd0b874e6f7c5852864c4c63c1477247",
        "published_date": null,
        "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:19:38.414534+00:00",
