        "title": "Quantum error correction below the surface code threshold | Nature",
        "snippet": "One potential source of excess correlations that we actively mitigate is leakage to higher excited states of our transmon qubits. During the logical qubit operation, we remove leakage from measure qubits using multilevel reset. For data qubits, DQLR swaps leakage excitations to measure qubits (or additional leakage removal qubits)[32](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR32 \"Miao, K. C. et al. Overcoming leakage in quantum error correction. Nat. Phys. 19, 1780–1786 (2023).\"). To examine sensitivity to leakage, we measure logical error probability of distance-3 and distance-5 codes in our 72-qubit processor with and without DQLR, and the results are shown in Fig. [2d](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#Fig2). Although activating DQLR does not strongly affect the distance-3 performance, it substanti",
