        "title": "Quantum error correction below the surface code threshold | Nature",
        "snippet": "ally boosts the distance-5 performance, resulting in a 35% increase in *Λ*. Comparatively, the detection probability decreases by only 12% ([Supplementary Information](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#MOESM1)), indicating that the detection probability is only a good proxy for logical error suppression if the errors are uncorrelated. Overall, we find that addressing leakage is crucial for operating surface codes with transmon qubits[15](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR15 \"Krinner, S. et al. Realizing repeated quantum error correction in a distance-three surface code. Nature 605, 669–674 (2022).\"),[32](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR32 \"Miao, K. C. et al. Overcoming leakage in quantum error correction. Nat. Phys. 19, 1780–1786 (2023).\"),[38](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR38 \"Varbano",
