        "snippet": "Averaging over bit- and phase-flip repetition codes, we obtain *Λ* = 8.4 ± 0.1 when fitting logical error per cycle versus code distance between *d* = 5 and *d* = 11 (Fig. [3a](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#Fig3)). Notably, the error per cycle on the 72-qubit processor is suppressed far below 10−6, breaking past the error floor observed previously. We attribute the mitigation of high-energy impact failures to gap-engineered Josephson junctions[39](/articles/s41586-024-08449-y#ref-CR39 \"McEwen, M. et al. Resisting high-energy impact events through gap engineering in superconducting qubit arrays. Phys. Rev. Lett. 133, 240601 (2024).\"). However, at code distances of *d* ≥ 15, we observe a deviation from exponential error suppression at high distances culminating in an apparent logical error fl",
