        "document_id": null,
        "title": "MIT engineers advance toward a fault-tolerant quantum computer | MIT News | Massachusetts Institute of Technology",
        "snippet": "He is joined on the paper by senior author Kevin O’Brien, an associate professor and principal investigator in the Research Laboratory of Electronics (RLE) at MIT who leads the Quantum Coherent Electronics Group in the Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS). Additional MIT co-authors, with affiliations in RLE and/or MIT Lincoln Laboratory, include Jeremy B. Kline, Alec Yen, Gregory Cunningham, Max Tan, Alicia Zang, Michael Gingras, Bethany M. Niedzielski, Hannah Stickler, Kyle Serniak, and Mollie E. Schwartz. The research [appears today in *Nature Communications*](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-59152-z).\n\n**A new coupler**\n\nThis physical demonstration builds on years of theoretical research in the O’Brien group.",
        "content_ref": "264139d80e7711afc820452de3bf5ee5c79b6aff585a9d7f9d1a26fa3c190881",
        "published_date": null,
