        "source_type": "passage",
        "provider": "direct_http",
        "url": "https://news.mit.edu/2025/mit-engineers-advance-toward-fault-tolerant-quantum-computer-0430",
        "document_id": null,
        "title": "MIT engineers advance toward a fault-tolerant quantum computer | MIT News | Massachusetts Institute of Technology",
        "snippet": "This quarton coupler is a special type of superconducting circuit that has the potential to generate extremely strong nonlinear coupling, which is essential for running most quantum algorithms. As the researchers feed more current into the coupler, it creates an even stronger nonlinear interaction. In this sense, nonlinearity means a system behaves in a way that is greater than the sum of its parts, exhibiting more complex properties.\n\n“Most of the useful interactions in quantum computing come from nonlinear coupling of light and matter. If you can get a more versatile range of different types of coupling, and increase the coupling strength, then you can essentially increase the processing speed of the quantum computer,” Ye explains.",
        "content_ref": "c589f63de275fd768ea346969dd5bc5e23df60ee4bc03332aea2551217e30307",
        "published_date": null,
        "retrieved_at": "2026-05-04T17:19:34.516819+00:00",
        "query": null,
        "quality_score": null,
        "freshness_score": null,
        "citation_id": null,
