0 ⟩ ⊗ ( w + v ) + | 1 ⟩ ⊗ ( w + v ) ) |\\psi_{\\text{anc}}\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle^{\\otimes(w+v)}+|1\\rangle^{\\otimes(w+v)}) for i = 1 i=1 to w w do Apply CNOT from d i d_{i} to ancilla i i end for Measure all w + v w+v ancillas → \\to outcomes { m 1 , … , m w + v } \\{m_{1},\\ldots,m_{w+v}\\} Compute parities: p j = m j ⊕ m j + 1 p_{j}=m_{j}\\oplus m_{j+1} for j = 1 , … , w + v − 1 j=1,\\ldots,w+v-1 if all p j = 0 p_{j}=0 then Accept syndrome s = m 1 s=m_{1} else Reject syndrome, retry or abort end if The parity checks verify that all ancillas are measured identically, confirming cat-state integrity. Failed verification indicates ancilla errors occurred during preparation or CNOTs, and the syndrome is unreliable. A.2 Steane Ancilla Preparation Preparing a logical | + L ⟩ |+_{L}\\rangle ancilla for Z-stabilizer measurement: Algorithm 4 Steane Ancilla Preparation with Verification 0: 7 physical ancilla qubits, swap policy (True/False) Initialize ancillas in | 0 ⟩ ⊗ 7 |0\\rangle^{\\otimes 7} Apply encoding circuit: H H on qubits 0, 1, 2, 3 CNOT cascade implementing Steane generator matrix Measure X-stabilizers and Z-stabilizers of ancilla if all stabilizers = +1 then Accept ancilla, proceed to syndrome measurement else if stabilizers indicate correctable error then Apply correction, verify again else if swap policy = True then Swap ancilla with data logical qubit Treat former data qubit as new ancilla else Discard ancilla, prepare a new one end if The swap policy is beneficial when ancilla preparation fidelity is lower than data qubit fidelity, allowing the high-quality data qubits to serve as fresh ancillas after measurement. Appendix B Additional Performance Data B.1 Extended Benchmark Results Table 3 provides complete benchmark data, including all measured quantities: Table 3 : Extended benchmark results with complete metrics for all test cases. Workload p phys p_{\\text{phys}} p log p_{\\text{log}} Fail Width Depth Shots n d n_{d} n a n_{a} n tot