        "quote": "Conventional QEC schemes use multiple physical qubits to encode a logical qubit, which not only requires a great number of hardware resources but also adds the number of error channels with increased number of physical qubits, resulting in ",
        "snippet_hash": "5d5f2da58ab6390aee95a73b519120c6568d88f626995b37f29910b5fe6f4f89"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.gmw.cn/2023-03/27/content_36457700.htm",
        "text": "As a result, they realized QEC of a logical qubit encoded with discrete photon number states in a single bosonic mode. Through repetitive real-time QEC operations, the storage lifetime of the quantum information has been extended beyond the break-even point.\n\nOther scientists involved in the study include Sun Luyan, an associate professor at Tsinghua University, and Zheng Shibiao, a professor at Fuzhou University.\n\nEditor:\nWXY\n\n\n\n[*![](https://img.gmw.cn/images/51990.files/images/001.png?v=1)*](javascript:void(0); \"Facebook\") ",
